  "caption": "Figure 2: The Graph Variational Causal Inference (graphVCI) framework for counterfactual generations. In a forward pass, the encoder takes graph G (e.g. gene relation graph), outcome Y (e.g. gene expressions), covariates X (e.g. cell types, donors) and treatment T (e.g. drug perturbation) as inputs and generates latent Z; (Z, T ) and (Z, T ′) where T ′ is the counterfactual treatment are separately passed into the decoder to attain reconstruction of Y and construction of counterfactual outcome Y ′ (note that the decoder estimates the conditional outcome distribution of Y ′, in which case T ′ need not necessarily be sampled according to a certain true distribution p(T ′|X) during optimization); Y ′ is then passed back into the encoder along with G , X , T ′ to attain counterfactual latent Z ′. The objective consists of the reconstruction loss of Y , the distribution loss of Y ′ and the KL-divergence between the conditional distributions of Z and Z ′.",
